12. Retention
Kafka typically retains records based on policies such as:
time
size
For example:
retain for 7 days
or:
retain until partition reaches configured size
Therefore:
Producer
   ↓
Kafka
   ↓
Consumer
is better understood as:
Producer
   ↓
Append to durable log
   ↓
Consumers independently read the log
This is why Kafka is often described as a distributed event log.
