17. Kafka is pull-based
This is important.
Conceptually:
Consumer
   |
   | FETCH
   ↓
Kafka
   |
   | records
   ↓
Consumer
The consumer generally pulls data rather than Kafka invoking the consumer for each message.
Why is this useful?
Because the consumer controls:
how much data it can process
when it fetches
how quickly it advances
This works well with batching and backpressure.
