19. One partition → one consumer within a group
For a given consumer group, a partition is normally assigned to only one consumer at a time.
Therefore:
4 partitions
4 consumers
can achieve:
P0 → C1
P1 → C2
P2 → C3
P3 → C4
But:
4 partitions
8 consumers
means some consumers have nothing assigned.
P0 → C1
P1 → C2
P2 → C3
P3 → C4

C5 → idle
C6 → idle
C7 → idle
C8 → idle
This leads to an important rule:
Within a consumer group, maximum useful parallelism is bounded by the number of partitions.
