40. The critical distinction
There are four different events that beginners often collapse into one:
1. Kafka stores record

2. Consumer fetches record

3. Application processes record

4. Consumer commits offset
They are separate.
For example:
Kafka stored
      ✓

Consumer fetched
      ✓

Application processed
      ✓

Offset committed
      ✗
A crash at this exact point can cause the record to be processed again.
That's the foundation for understanding:
•	at-most-once
•	at-least-once
•	exactly-once
•	offset commits
