20. Why duplicate processing can happen
Suppose:
P0:

100
101
102
103
Consumer C1 processes:
100 ✓
101 ✓
102 ✓
but crashes before committing its progress.
After rebalance:
P0 → C2
C2 resumes from the last committed offset.
It may process:
102
103
again.
So rebalancing interacts directly with offset management.
That's why you should study these concepts together:
Consumer Groups
       +
Rebalancing
       +
Offsets
