29. Important distinction: broker vs coordinator
Suppose:
Broker 1
Broker 2
Broker 3
A consumer might fetch:
P0 → Broker 1
P1 → Broker 2
P2 → Broker 3
But the group coordinator might be:
Broker 2
That doesn't mean all data flows through Broker 2.
The coordinator is responsible for group coordination.
Partition data comes from the relevant partition leaders.
So:
Coordinator
   ↓
group membership/coordination
while:
Partition leader
   ↓
partition data
Again: don't mix these responsibilities.
