41. University-level distributed systems connection
Kafka replication is teaching you several general distributed-systems concepts:
Replicated state
same logical log
        ↓
multiple physical replicas
Failure detection
broker unavailable
       ↓
system detects failure
Leadership
one replica coordinates writes
Quorum-like durability
enough in-sync replicas
       ↓
safe acknowledgement
Failure-domain awareness
independent physical failures
       ↓
independent replicas
CAP-style trade-offs
When replicas disappear:
availability
      ↕
consistency / durability
Kafka is therefore an excellent system to study after learning generic distributed systems.
