The 5 concepts I want you to internalize first
Before moving to Exchange Types, make sure these are crystal clear:
1. Producer does NOT normally publish directly to a queue.

2. Exchange performs routing.

3. Queue stores/holds messages for consumers.

4. ACK means "this delivery was successfully handled",
   not "this business operation can never happen again."

5. RabbitMQ provides messaging guarantees;
   your application must provide business idempotency.
If those five ideas are solid, the rest of RabbitMQ becomes much easier.
