24. Deep system-design question: Exchange vs Queue
This distinction is worth memorizing.
Suppose you have:
Payment Service
Inventory Service
Analytics Service
Should you create:
Option A
One queue
    |
    +--> Payment
    +--> Inventory
    +--> Analytics
or:
Option B
Exchange
   |
   +--> payment.q
   +--> inventory.q
   +--> analytics.q
Usually B if these are independent services.
Why?
With A:
payment consumes message
then Inventory may never see that same message.
They're competing consumers.
With B:
payment.q      → Payment
inventory.q    → Inventory
analytics.q    → Analytics
each gets its own copy.
This is one of the most important RabbitMQ topology decisions.
