45. The key interview distinction
If an interviewer asks:
"How do I broadcast a message to five services?"
Don't say:
"Create five consumers."
That's wrong.
You want:
Exchange
   |
   +--> Queue A → Consumer(s)
   +--> Queue B → Consumer(s)
   +--> Queue C → Consumer(s)
   +--> Queue D → Consumer(s)
   +--> Queue E → Consumer(s)
Why?
Because five consumers on one queue means:
one message → one consumer
Five queues bound to the exchange means:
one message → five consumer groups
That distinction is fundamental.
