42. RabbitMQ vs Kafka connection
Since you're learning system design at university depth, you should recognize an important architectural similarity.
Kafka naturally exposes:
Topic
  ↓
Partitions
  ↓
Consumers
RabbitMQ traditionally centers around:
Exchange
  ↓
Queues
  ↓
Consumers
But with RabbitMQ routing/partitioning patterns, you can construct:
Exchange
   ↓
partitioned queues
   ↓
consumers
So conceptually:
Kafka partition
≈
RabbitMQ partition-style queue
but the systems are not equivalent.
Their storage models, consumption models, replay semantics, ordering semantics, operational models, and intended workloads differ.
We'll cover that comparison later.
